    description: "FOUND 2026-10-03 while sweeping WI-nakur's family (values that reach a producer keyword through data, not a literal), on branch jgstern-agent/fix/nakur.\n\nyaml_ansible.py (packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/yaml_ansible.py, the include/import edge in process_mapping_pairs) emits\n\n    if key in (\"include_tasks\", \"import_tasks\", \"include_role\", \"import_role\"):\n        ... Edge.create(..., edge_type=\"imports\", evidence_type=key, ...)\n\nso the evidence_type is one of those four YAML keys. None of the four is in the evidence-type registry (evidence_types.all_evidence_type_names()).\n\nLIVE REPRO (worktree ~/hg_wt/nakur, PYTHONPATH pinned): a 3-file playbook with `include_tasks: setup.yml` produced one edge `imports`, meta.evidence_type = \"include_tasks\", find_evidence_type(\"include_tasks\") is None. (`include_role` with a mapping value emitted no edge in that fixture; not chased.)\n\nWHY NO GATE SEES IT: `key` comes from the parsed YAML (a tree-sitter call result), so it is unenumerable; only the STATEMENT-LEVEL guard `if key in (...)` bounds it. hypergumbo_core.value_flow (WI-nakur) narrows an IfExp arm by ==/in tests, not a name used inside an `if` block, so the L3 ratchet stays green. This is the one remaining unresolvable evidence_type site in an analyzer besides re-emission copies.\n\nNOT CHECKED: whether any consumer branches on these values; whether other analyzers use the same \"guard-narrowed key as evidence_type\" shape (value_flow's unresolved list for evidence_type after WI-nakur is: receiver_type_dispatch.py evidence_type, yaml_ansible.py key, yaml_ansible.py edge.evidence_type).\n\nDECISION NEEDED: register the four (axis + no seed, the WI-nubuv/WI-pubin precedent) or fold to one registered pathway (e.g. `include`, already registered) with the directive kept in meta. And either teach value_flow statement-level narrowing (`if x in (lits):` dominating the use, no rebinding in between) or file it as its own residual."  # b132
    fields: {}  # b132
